---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
The return trip of a pin: where the pull requests `test-requirements.txt` pins stand, and once every one is merged and released for the target, the `[DON'T MERGE]` commit dropped. `--push` sends the branch to its pull request, `--merge` merges that once its checks are green

Usage: odx migrate unpin [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --to <SERIES>
          The target series the dependencies must be released for [default: the series the migration branch's name starts with]

      --pr <PR>
          The pull request of the branch, for example `OCA/contract#1234` [default: the one `odx migrate pr` or `odx migrate update` recorded]

      --check
          Only say where the pins stand; change nothing

      --push
          Then push the branch where its pull request comes from

      --merge
          Then merge the pull request, when no pin is left, the branch is pushed and its checks are green. Nothing is merged without this flag

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only; a repository not in the cache yet is still fetched. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only
